  "externalFindings": {
    "identity": "Dutch-taught full-time standard ACTA Dentistry bachelor. The registry target is VU Amsterdam within ACTA, the joint dental faculty of VU Amsterdam and the University of Amsterdam. The annual regulations effective 1 September 2026 apply to registered students; the annual catalogue supplies exact units and credits.",
    "creditCoverage": "OER Article 11.3 and TB_TANDHK agree on 10, 12 and 11 positive-credit units and 60 EC per year. The zero-credit Dutch test is integrated into Introduction. Professional conduct is already included. No standard open elective block. The individual free degree and honours are separate and are excluded.",
    "progression": "Article 9.1 sets early oral biology and caries, direct restorations, skills 1A and New Patient practical attendance in 1B before year-two prevention and skills 2A. Skills 2B also requires passed 1B and attendance at 2A. Year-three prevention and treatment follows passed year-two prevention, care planning, periodontitis, prevention line and both skills lines. The 14 EC placement requires passed year-one research methods and year-two research preparation.",
    "additionalRequirements": "Articles 10.4 and 11 govern Dutch test or remediation, at least 90% practical attendance, preclinical preparation before patient treatment, and competence reassessment after a prolonged treatment interruption. First-year positive study advice requires 42 EC.",
    "placement": "The exact 2026–2027 T_B3WSTAGE entry confirms supervised dental or related biomedical research or extended literature study, usually with another student, with a thesis and oral defence. Execution, thesis and presentation are separately passed. The assessment paragraph uses an alternate block label, while the exact code, name, credits and prerequisites agree with the OER."
  },
